  "question": {
    "text": "An electron revolving in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mtext>th </mtext></msup></math> Bohr orbit has magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>∝</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Magnetic moment of electron is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Clearly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
